Third-party code

The reconstructed kernel in 07_kernel/ adopts reference code where the
compiled result matches the original OPENSTEP 4.2 kernel bytes. Code taken
from those references, whole files or marked lines inside other files, is NOT
relicensed by the BSD 2-Clause License above. It stays under the licence of
the code it came from, and the notices it carries are kept with it.

The origin of every adopted file (repository or archive, revision, path) and
its licence are recorded in 07_kernel/PROVENANCE.tsv; changes made to
reference code are listed in 07_kernel/MODIFICATIONS.md. Where a file header
or its PROVENANCE.tsv entry names a third-party origin, that origin's licence
governs that file or the marked part of it.

The references used are:

  - Darwin 0.1 (Apple Computer, Inc.): Apple Public Source License 1.0, see
    07_kernel/LICENSES/APSL-1.0.txt. Some Darwin 0.1 files carry other
    notices instead (for example the University of California BSD licence);
    the notice in the file applies.
  - Mach 4 (Carnegie Mellon University; University of Utah): the CMU and
    Utah notices in the files, see 07_kernel/LICENSES/CMU-UTAH-MACH4.txt and
    07_kernel/LICENSES/CMU-MACH.txt.
  - NeXTMach mk-108.1 (NeXT, Carnegie Mellon University, the Regents of the
    University of California): the notices carried in the files.
  - Net/2 (the Regents of the University of California): the BSD licence
    notices carried in the files.

Files generated by tools (for example MIG output and configuration headers)
follow the licence of their inputs as recorded in 07_kernel/PROVENANCE.tsv.

Not covered and not included

  - The original OPENSTEP 4.2 kernel binaries, the OPENSTEP 4.2 SDK header
    copies and the reference source archives are not distributed in this
    repository (see README.md, "What is not in this repository").
  - NeXT, OPENSTEP, Apple and other names and marks belong to their owners.
    Screenshots under docs/images/ show OPENSTEP software running in an
    emulator; the software shown is not licensed by this file.
